consumer(path=>path.includes('.resourceFieldRef'),'A zero divisor becomes quantity 1 in the extractor. CPU scales MilliValue and other supported resources scale Value; results round upward with math.Ceil. A nonempty container name searches regular then init containers and fails if absent. Downward volume extraction deep-copies the found container and fills absent or zero CPU/memory/ephemeral-storage limits from node allocatable before scaling; environment extraction without an explicit name reads the current container.',[source('pkg/api/v1/resource/helpers.go','80-205','The original resource extractor implements container lookup, zero divisor fallback, ceiling scaling and node-allocatable limit fallback.'),source('pkg/kubelet/kubelet_pods.go','1026-1037','Environment resource selection uses current-container extraction for an empty name.')],['exact runtime scaling fallback','Exact scaling for zero']);
consumer(path=>path===`${p}.automountServiceAccountToken`||path===`${p}.serviceAccountName`||path.startsWith(`${p}.imagePullSecrets`),'On created Pod admission, an empty serviceAccountName becomes default; lookup errors forbid admission. Pod automount preference wins over ServiceAccount preference, then defaults true. With token mounting enabled and this effective preference true, admission adds token mounts unless the mount path is already used. If imagePullSecrets is empty, admission copies ServiceAccount imagePullSecrets; a nonempty authored list is retained.',[source('plugin/pkg/admission/serviceaccount/admission.go','148-176','ServiceAccount admission defaults and resolves the account, mounts permitted tokens and fills only an empty imagePullSecrets list.'),source('plugin/pkg/admission/serviceaccount/admission.go','254-265','Automount precedence is Pod, ServiceAccount, then true.')],['ServiceAccount admission plugin','Image pull credential selection']);
consumer(path=>['priority','priorityClassName','preemptionPolicy'].some(x=>path===`${p}.${x}`),'Created Pod Priority admission resolves the named class or the global default. A missing named class rejects admission. A supplied numerical priority differing from the computed class value rejects admission; otherwise admission writes the computed value. When the class supplies preemptionPolicy, a different authored policy rejects admission and the class policy is written. Pod update fills only omitted values from stored values; immutable Pod validation still applies.',[source('plugin/pkg/admission/priority/admission.go','137-204','Priority admission distinguishes create class resolution/conflicts from update preservation.'),source('plugin/pkg/admission/priority/admission.go','228-256','Default priority chooses a global default class or zero.')],['Priority admission']);
consumer(path=>path===`${p}.runtimeClassName`||path.startsWith(`${p}.overhead`)||path.startsWith(`${p}.nodeSelector`),'Created Pod RuntimeClass admission performs cache then API lookup; a missing named class rejects admission. Class overhead replaces absent/empty authored overhead but a different nonempty map rejects admission; validation rejects nonnil Pod overhead with no corresponding class overhead. Class node selectors merge with authored keys, reject differing values for the same key, and add nonconflicting keys; class tolerations merge with Pod tolerations.',[source('plugin/pkg/admission/runtimeclass/admission.go','142-238','RuntimeClass admission implements lookup, exact overhead conflicts and node selector/toleration merge.')],['RuntimeClass admission lookup','RuntimeClass admission can supply overhead']);
consumer(path=>/\.affinity\.pod(?:Anti)?Affinity/.test(path),'Affinity terms match Pod labels AND the union of explicitly listed namespaces and namespace-selector matches. When the namespace list is empty and namespaceSelector is nil, the scheduler inserts the incoming Pod namespace. A nonnil empty namespace selector selects every namespace; nil selects none through the general converter. Required incoming terms resolve a nonempty namespace selector into the namespace-name set before filtering.',[source('staging/src/k8s.io/kube-scheduler/framework/types.go','377-391','AffinityTerm matches namespace membership or namespace-selector labels together with Pod selector.'),source('staging/src/k8s.io/kube-scheduler/framework/types.go','419-445','Affinity term conversion and own-namespace fallback depend on nil selector and empty namespace list.'),source('pkg/scheduler/framework/plugins/interpodaffinity/plugin.go','137-157','Incoming term namespace-selector results merge into the explicit namespace set.'),source('pkg/scheduler/framework/plugins/interpodaffinity/filtering.go','274-309','Required incoming affinity and anti-affinity namespace sets are prepared before filtering.')],['Exact scheduler fallback','scheduler-specific namespace fallback']);
consumer(path=>path.includes('.affinity.nodeAffinity'),'Node affinity ORs terms and ANDs each term label and field requirements. Empty terms select no nodes. Gt/Lt requires exactly one base-10 signed int64 value at selector construction; missing or nonnumeric node label values do not match. Gt is strictly greater and Lt strictly less. A parse error is returned only if no alternative term matches.',[source('staging/src/k8s.io/component-helpers/scheduling/corev1/nodeaffinity/nodeaffinity.go','61-105','Empty terms are skipped and alternatives use lazy OR matching.'),source('staging/src/k8s.io/component-helpers/scheduling/corev1/nodeaffinity/nodeaffinity.go','202-253','Node requirements convert to the concrete label selector operators.'),source('staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/labels/selector.go','185-215','Gt/Lt construction parses one decimal int64 operand.'),source('staging/src/k8s.io/apimachinery/pkg/labels/selector.go','265-292','Gt/Lt matching requires a present parseable node label and strict integer comparison.')],['Empty node-selector terms require','Gt/Lt parsing']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${p}.topologySpreadConstraints`),'The scheduler converts the label selector and ANDs equality requirements for matchLabelKeys present in the incoming Pod labels; absent Pod-label keys add no requirement. Nil minDomains uses 1, nil nodeAffinityPolicy uses Honor and nil nodeTaintsPolicy uses Ignore. Enabled inclusion policies apply their retained overrides. Honor filters node affinity or untolerated scheduling taints; Ignore omits that respective filter.',[source('pkg/scheduler/framework/plugins/podtopologyspread/common.go','42-55','Honor inclusion policies filter node affinity and taints.'),source('pkg/scheduler/framework/plugins/podtopologyspread/common.go','86-142','Concrete spread selector, matched label keys and nil policy/min-domain defaults are constructed here.')],['Scheduler selector construction is a separate','Every topology-spread child']);
consumer(path=>path.includes('.affinity')||path.startsWith(`${p}.topologySpreadConstraints`),'API preparation drops match/mismatch keys if the associated feature is disabled and not already in use by the old spec. Retained selectors and keys receive the selected strict or old-object compatibility options; a disabled gate is not permission to infer that a supplied retained field reached the scheduler.',[source('pkg/api/pod/util.go','1164-1205','Feature-dependent field dropping distinguishes Pod affinity and topology spread.'),source('pkg/api/pod/util.go','417-485','Validation options combine gates with old-selector compatibility.')],['Each key item and exact merge','Complete recursive node-selector']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.emptyDir`),'The emptyDir plugin accepts the default medium, Memory or a hugepage medium; other media fail setup with unknown storage medium. Memory size is the minimum positive applicable bound of node allocatable memory, Pod memory limit and authored sizeLimit; zero sizeLimit does not lower it. Setup mounts tmpfs/hugetlbfs or creates a directory and applies group ownership. Disk quota assignment depends on filesystem support; this path is not a universal hard disk-capacity limit.',[source('pkg/volume/emptydir/empty_dir.go','114-165','Memory emptyDir size selection excludes zero and uses node/Pod/volume bounds.'),source('pkg/volume/emptydir/empty_dir.go','234-317','Setup chooses supported media, ownership and optional filesystem quota assignment.'),source('pkg/volume/emptydir/empty_dir.go','318-388','Memory and hugepage volume mount construction uses the chosen size and page size.')],['Storage medium support','Node medium support','API acceptance does not establish']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(trust),'The informer trust manager requires synchronized cache. Named NotFound or zero signer/selector matches returns empty data only with optional true; other lookup/conversion errors fail. Signer selection converts nil labelSelector to match nothing and {} to match everything, then filters by exact signerName. Cache entries are normalized/deduplicated and refreshed through informer invalidation. A no-op manager returns an unsupported-operation error.',[source('pkg/kubelet/clustertrustbundle/clustertrustbundle_manager.go','169-194','Informer events invalidate normalized trust cache entries.'),source('pkg/kubelet/clustertrustbundle/clustertrustbundle_manager.go','197-280','Actual trust lookup selects name or signer/labels and implements missing-result handling.'),source('pkg/kubelet/clustertrustbundle/clustertrustbundle_manager.go','326-335','A no-op trust manager rejects trust lookups.')],['Feature enablement, bundle existence','General nil-selector conversion']);
refine(`${trust}.labelSelector`,{omitted:'With signerName, nil is passed through the manager converter and matches no bundles; without optional true, the empty result fails. With name, nil is required.',emptyValue:'With signerName, {} selects all labels before exact signerName filtering. With name, every nonnil selector is forbidden.'});
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(cert),'The issuing manager creates a keypair for keyType and submits a PodCertificateRequest with Pod, ServiceAccount and node identity, signerName, authored maximum lifetime pointer and annotations. Lookup is indexed by Pod UID, volume and source position; absent credentials fail until issuance supplies a valid state. The no-op manager returns unimplemented. Key bytes and issued certificate bytes are separate from API acceptance.',[source('pkg/kubelet/podcertificate/podcertificatemanager.go','736-820','Certificate request construction forwards exact identity/source settings and bundle retrieval fails before credentials exist.'),source('pkg/kubelet/podcertificate/podcertificatemanager.go','987-997','No-op certificate manager is an explicit unavailable-operation boundary.')],['Certificate issuance, feature gates']);
consumer(path=>path.includes('.affinity.podAffinity')||path.includes('.affinity.podAntiAffinity')||path.startsWith(`${p}.topologySpreadConstraints`),'On Pod create, enabled API selector mutation appends In requirements for matchLabelKeys and NotIn requirements for mismatchLabelKeys whose keys exist in Pod labels. Absent keys add no expression; a nil selector remains match-none. Topology selector mutation additionally requires both topology MatchLabelKeys and selector-merge gates. Added expressions AND with the authored selector.',[source('pkg/registry/core/pod/strategy.go','857-925','Pod-create selector mutation looks up incoming Pod labels and appends In/NotIn requirements conditionally.')]);
const unsupportedSources=['cephfs','flocker','glusterfs','photonPersistentDisk','quobyte','rbd','scaleIO','storageos'];
consumer(path=>unsupportedSources.some(branch=>path===`${v}.${branch}`||path.startsWith(`${v}.${branch}.`)),'This retained historical source can pass API validation, but the pinned standard kubelet does not register an implementation for this branch and it is not one of the listed CSI migrations. Volume plugin selection therefore fails instead of mounting it. Blocked step: mount this source with the standard binary. Safe action: have the storage operator select a supported CSI/PVC source and rewrite the manifest. Owner: cluster storage operator. Follow-up: verify the replacement driver is registered and the replacement Pod volume reaches successful mount before application startup.',[source('cmd/kubelet/app/plugins.go','28-83','The standard binary enumerates its volume plugins, including CSI and supported in-tree branches.'),source('cmd/kubelet/app/plugins_providers.go','59-70','The remaining provider registration is Portworx, controlled by its unregister feature.'),source('pkg/volume/csimigration/plugin_manager.go','56-108','Only enumerated legacy providers have a CSI migration route.'),source('pkg/volume/plugins.go','631-665','Plugin selection returns ErrNoPluginMatched if no registered plugin supports the spec.')],['external or migrated storage driver','Each optional source child','Driver installation, backend','Secret existence, type']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.csi`),'For inline CSI, the node requires Ephemeral lifecycle support in CSIDriver. The mounter passes fsType, volumeAttributes and readOnly to NodePublishVolume. A nodePublishSecretRef is resolved in the Pod namespace; every Secret data byte value is converted to a string map for the driver, without an API-level fixed credential-key schema. Lookup failure is a transient mount failure. Driver RPC failure fails setup; API acceptance alone does not establish a driver/backend mount.',[source('pkg/volume/csi/csi_mounter.go','120-176','Inline CSI uses Ephemeral lifecycle and namespace-local NodePublishSecretRef.'),source('pkg/volume/csi/csi_mounter.go','217-251','Node-publish credentials and selected Pod token attributes are prepared.'),source('pkg/volume/csi/csi_mounter.go','300-335','The actual NodePublishVolume call passes the effective readOnly/fsType/attributes/secret fields and handles errors.'),source('pkg/volume/csi/csi_util.go','45-56','Secret credentials copy every data entry as a string.')],['CSIDriver lifecycle modes','external or migrated storage driver','Secret existence, type']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.secret`)||path.startsWith(`${v}.configMap`)||path.startsWith(`${projection}.secret`)||path.startsWith(`${projection}.configMap`),'The kubelet object managers choose API reads, TTL cache or informer watch propagation. Plugins reassemble file payloads on remount and use an atomic writer, so manager propagation and the next remount determine update visibility. A subPath mount binds the selected path separately; rewriting the parent volume payload does not replace the existing bind mount. Optional applies only to the stated missing-object/key paths, not arbitrary API errors.',[source('pkg/kubelet/secret/secret_manager.go','116-161','Caching and watching Secret managers define retrieval/propagation routes.'),source('pkg/kubelet/configmap/configmap_manager.go','114-160','Caching and watching ConfigMap managers define retrieval/propagation routes.'),source('pkg/volume/util/atomic_writer.go','86-120','Atomic writer publishes new payload data through timestamp directories and symlink replacement.')],['Existence, key selection, optional handling','Refresh, subPath update visibility']);
consumer(path=>path.startsWith(`${v}.downwardAPI`)||path.startsWith(`${projection}.downwardAPI`),'Downward payload construction reads the created Pod fields, cleans each output path, selects the per-item mode over fallback mode and aggregates extraction errors. Duplicate paths in a direct downwardAPI payload use the later map write; projected explicit duplicates are rejected by API validation. Updating Pod fields is observed only when the plugin collects and republishes a new payload.',[source('pkg/volume/downwardapi/downwardapi.go','238-277','CollectData performs exact path/mode selection, field/resource extraction and map writes.')],['runtime extractor and file update']);
